{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10589-crossover-questions","id":10589,"title":"Crossover Questions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-14T11:22:50-08:00","id":10589,"title":"Crossover Questions.","content":"Taking Matt's advice to move this question here so it doesn't get lost in the jumble of Kickstarter comments, here it goes:<br /> <span style=\"color:#0B1902\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Does Disquiet effect demons? I'd imagine that it does, seeing that demons are more in tune with the physics and metaphysics of the world they'd realize quicker then other spalts that something is off about them.<br /> <br /> Second question: Say a demon is coerced via Dominate or some other mind effecting power to tell the truth do tehy actually have to tell the truth or can they use liars tongue to make a false statement true and thus fulfill the vampires command?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T12:19:57-08:00","id":10670,"title":"","content":"Demons are,after a fashion, humans, so Disquiet effects them as normal. Nothing indicates they'd have an increased awareness of it working on them or anything of the like.<br /> <br /> As for the second, I have no idea, but I assume Liar's Tongue allows the cirucmvention of &quot;Tell me the Truth&quot; things. Demons have weird, quantum brains, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T12:37:13-08:00","id":10683,"title":"","content":"only thing is they still have a supernatural resistance (dont know the disquiet rules if there is some roll involved or something)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:25:35-08:00","id":10719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10589-crossover-questions?p=10683#post10683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">only thing is they still have a supernatural resistance (dont know the disquiet rules if there is some roll involved or something)</div> </div> </div> </div>Disquiet rules are Resolve+Composure vs Azoth with modifiers for both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:33:57-08:00","id":10727,"title":"","content":"interesting hmmmm can it be that cover adds to resolve+composure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:40:41-08:00","id":10733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10589-crossover-questions?p=10727#post10727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">interesting hmmmm can it be that cover adds to resolve+composure?</div> </div> </div> </div>It cannot, being that Supernatural Tolerance Traits generally only add to rolls of singular Resistance Attributes and our one example of a Demon interacting with a Promethean mentions its eventual inexplicable-even-to-itself decision to murder the Created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:50:22-08:00","id":10742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10589-crossover-questions?p=10733#post10733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It cannot, being that Supernatural Tolerance Traits generally only add to rolls of singular Resistance Attributes and our one example of a Demon interacting with a Promethean mentions its eventual inexplicable-even-to-itself decision to murder the Created.</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly it would be a danger to Cover for the Demon to <b>not </b>be affected. Though, now that I say that, I might be more interesting for Demons to be immune, but have to hate on the Prommie anyway to maintain their cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T14:09:50-08:00","id":10766,"title":"","content":"So where does that leave Demons that have been Burned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T14:15:41-08:00","id":10771,"title":"","content":"How do demonic powers interact with a deathless's Memory? specifically, a) when the demon first falls and memories get rewritten, does that still affect the Mummy and b) are mummies affected by the Memory Theif demon form power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T19:30:23-08:00","id":10998,"title":"","content":"An option for prometheans in crossovers is that disquiet is just for mortals, so there's that, another optional rule is that supernaturals can fight disquiet with suitable powers like a mage's mind magic.<br /> <br /> For demons, there's Cool heads prevail, miles away, force relationship, Sermon could make acting on disquiet a breaking point, and the mental resistance demonic form power would help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T21:49:15-08:00","id":11059,"title":"","content":"Quick question after reading the section of the Demon Preview Book Thing dealing with &quot;other creations of the God-Machine&quot;. It mentions <i>qashmallim</i> as being a creation of the God-Machine, which would imply that the Principle and the God-Machine are the same thing. Thing is, I get two very different vibes from the two. The God-Machine gives me a very &quot;Stasis and Redundancy&quot; feeling, whereas the Principle gives me more of an impression of &quot;Spontaneity and Risk&quot;. In other words, the God-Machine seems cautious and dedicated to the status quo, whereas the Principle has always seemed to be more daring and actively against the status quo. Were the devs intending to imply that the Principle and the God-Machine are the same thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T22:00:33-08:00","id":11063,"title":"","content":"Well it says that some demons believe that. There's no concrete evidence for it like there is for angels and demons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T22:00:37-08:00","id":11064,"title":"","content":"What pages were you reading? If they were pp. 70-71, you came away with a very different impression than I did of that passage, which states explicitly the differing agendas of the God-Machine and the &quot;different set of principles&quot; <i>qashmallim</i> serve, qualifies the origin of <i>qashmallim</i> with &quot;some demons believe,&quot; and generally refers to them as not angels in the same sense that the God-Machine's ephemeral servants are angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T22:10:31-08:00","id":11068,"title":"","content":"...after reading it a second time, I admit that my initial reading was wrong. It does, indeed, say that certain demons believe it and that there's no evidence for it. So... yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T15:29:06-08:00","id":11627,"title":"","content":"Furthermore, it strongly implies that the Principle is <i>not</i> the God-Machine, in that the <i>qashmallim</i> serve the former instead of the latter. <br /> <br /> I personally rather like the gnostic interpretation where the God-Machine takes on the role of the Demiurge while the Principle takes on the role of the Creator, with <i>qashmallim</i> being the Principle\u2019s agents of evolution and entropy while angels are the God-Machines agents of the status quo. <br /> <br /> I also find it interesting that this topic has thus far focused on <b>Demon</b> and <b>Promethean</b>; traditionally, crossover topics have tended to feature <b>Mage</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T15:39:14-08:00","id":11633,"title":"","content":"I think that might be at least partially owed to the presence of the Qashmallim as antagonists in the Demon proof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:55:13-08:00","id":11736,"title":"","content":"Personally, I get the feeling from what I have read in Demon so far (only about a third of the way through) that it crosses over with some games better then others.<br /> <br /> As Dataweaver said, Mage has a habit of being the game that pretty much everything (expect maybe Hunter) crosses over with the most. This makes sense as Mage has the largest scope and arguably the widest themes of any of the games. Likewise, the protagonists of that game are expected to &quot;poke&quot; the unknown, the unusual and the weird and their magic lets them work out certain things about other supernaturals (like their existence and a hint of their nature and abilities) reasonably easily. As I final point, Mage is concerned with a metaphysical architecture that the other games simply do not either require or engage with and has a history to match that can be actively referenced and used (unlike Vampire (which lacks it) or Werewolf (which uses a more &quot;folklore&quot; and parable approach).<br /> <br /> Its not surprising then that Mage is one of the games I feel can cross-over most naturally with Demon and could work as a long-term mixed campaign. The two compliment each other well and have certain tool sets that make them different enough to feel they both contribute in different ways. Interestingly both have consequences for the use of their power, more so then the other games lines. So Abyssal Intrusions and Angels appearing are always a possibility to spice things up (or God-Machine forbid, both at once). If you want to involve history that's fine. Demon lacks it and the God-Machine can slot into a number of different points in Mage history. <br /> <br /> Promethean is usually the black sheep of cross-over's. Disquiet and the Wasteland effect are buggers to get around. Likewise, Promethean is a deeply personal game at its core. The journey of a potential person into full person hood. My players often joke its &quot;The best game you will never play&quot;. Yet, in Demon I think Promethean finally has another game that really resonates with it in a way beyond a simple theme similarity (personhood with Changeling, youth vs age with Mummy). Demon's could sidestep the Disquite and they can be mobile enough that the Wasteland would not be such an issue. Likewise, the number of ways that the God Machine and Principle might relate and interact has a dozen plot hooks and interpretations in it. <br /> <br /> The third game that really resonates for cross-over purposes is Changeling. A number of games cross-over well with Changeling. Hunter for the humanist tones, Mummy for thematics revolving around identity, Mage for the mystery, magic and possibilities. Demon I think goes beyond these other though. To go along with the espionage metaphors rife in Demon, if Demons are burned spies from the CIA then Changelings are burned spies from the KGB. The two games have a lot of interesting parallels but a number of points of divergence to make the contrasts generate really interesting in-game scenes and narratives. <br /> <br /> Obviously these are just my observations, I would be fascinated to hear about what other people thing about Demons potential to cross over with the others lines in interesting ways. For example, I don't see a huge amount of mileage in crossing Demon over with Hunter. Yet part of me wants to do something interesting with the Lucifuge in some way. In particular something to do with THE LUCIFUGE herself. I remember talks on the RPG.net threads about Satan/Lucifer as &quot;a signal. I wonder who keeps that signal running? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}